<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ionian University of Smyrna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1920–1922</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ionian University of Smyrna was a Greek university planned in Smyrna during the Greek administration of the city after 1919. The mathematician <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantin-caratheodory">Constantin Carathéodory</a> was appointed to organise it in 1920, and buildings, staff and a library were prepared, but it never opened: the Greek army's defeat and the Turkish capture of Smyrna in September 1922 ended the project.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ionian-university-of-smyrna.jpg" alt="Ionian University of Smyrna" width="320" height="185" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ionian_University_of_Smyrna.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
